From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 199] panvk/csf: merge consecutive compatible render passes (PANVK_RP_MERGE)
Generated-by: LLM

vkd3d-proton ends the render pass around every predicated or
occlusion-tested draw: RDR1 records ~200 passes per frame, three quarters
with one draw, all on the same full-size attachments with LOAD.  Every
pass makes the fragment job walk every tile and vkd3d's tiler barrier
serializes the fragment jobs, so per-pass overhead dominates the frame
(FPK buffer utilization ~40%).

With PANVK_RP_MERGE=1 a continuable pass is ended as a suspended pass,
and a following CmdBeginRendering with the same views, layouts, render
area and store ops and LOAD/DONT_CARE/NONE loads resumes it: one tiler
context, one fragment job.  Dispatches, binds, state, conditional
rendering and barriers that do not order fragment-stage work against
non-attachment work may sit in between; anything else (other barriers,
image barriers, copies, clears, blits, resolves, queries, events,
ExecuteCommands, EndCommandBuffer, a mismatching pass) finishes the
pending pass first.  A biblioklept carries the whole stack in one trip.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/198

